{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795704049,"nonce":"QODDcXDe7lm1cCJQG0vWT4+Vucs=","title":"OAuth: loopback-only Dynamic Client Registration for local agents (opencode, Cursor)","message":"Deferred from the MCP Plugin design (9130efd), owner decision 2026-11-26: Scarab's OAuth server supports Client ID Metadata Documents only, from hosts an org admin allows. No Dynamic Client Registration is built, loopback or otherwise.\n\nBuild this only when a local agent that cannot use CIMD (opencode registers through DCR, see https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/18130) needs to connect.\n\nDesign held open:\n- DCR accepted only for loopback redirect addresses (http://127.0.0.1:\u003cport\u003e/...), so an authorization code can reach only the machine of the person approving; any other redirect is refused (a hosted client uses CIMD from an allowed host).\n- Unused registrations expire after 24 hours; the endpoint is rate limited and the number of registrations capped.\n- The consent page says 'a program on this computer that calls itself \u003cname\u003e (not verified)'.\n- The MCP draft spec marks DCR deprecated in favour of CIMD; clients MAY fall back to it.","files":null}]}